---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout
  title="Talks - Manuel Gil - Open Source Maintainer"
  description="Talks and events where I've shared what I've learned about open source and the tools I've built."
  keywords="talks, communities, developer, open source"
>
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 pt-20">
    <section class="flex items-center justify-center py-28">
      <div class="max-w-3xl text-center">
        <h1
          class="mb-4 bg-linear-to-r from-primary to-accent bg-clip-text text-6xl font-bold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-transparent"
        >
          Talks
        </h1>
        <p class="mb-8 text-xl text-zinc-400">
          I speak at events sometimes, when I have something worth sharing.
          Mostly about open source and the tools I've built.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto mb-32 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-bold">Where I've Spoken</h2>
        <ul class="mb-6 space-y-6 text-zinc-400">
          <li>
            <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
            <strong class="text-zinc-200"
              >CCOSS (Open Source Software Contributors Summit)</strong
            > — Talked about open source contributions and what it looks like in practice.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
            <strong class="text-zinc-200">FLISoL, Nerdearla, and local meetups</strong> — Sessions
            about VSCode extensions, automation, and open source workflows. Small rooms and
            virtual calls.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
            <strong class="text-zinc-200">Conversations after talks</strong> — Some useful
            things started with someone asking a question after a session.
            The informal part matters.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mb-6 text-zinc-400">
          I don't speak on a schedule. I do it when I have something honest to say and someone
          invites me to say it. The best part is always the questions I didn't expect.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://sessionize.com/imgildev"
          class="text-primary transition-colors hover:text-primary-dark"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Speaker profile on Sessionize →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
